# .worktreeinclude — files copied into every new isolated worktree.
#
# When an agent is dispatched with `isolation: worktree` (see agents/builder.md),
# the platform creates a fresh git worktree for that run. A worktree only
# contains tracked files, so anything gitignored (local env files, local
# secrets, local override config) is missing by default and the isolated
# builder cannot run or verify its work.
#
# List one path per line, gitignore syntax, relative to the project root.
# Every path listed here is copied from the main working tree into each new
# worktree at creation time, so isolated builders get the same local config
# a normal working-tree run would have. Keep this list to local, non-secret
# config where possible; anything genuinely sensitive still belongs in a
# managed secret store, not a copied file (see rules/ai-safety-rules.md and
# secrets-patterns.md (Compliance controls section) for what must never live in a plain file).
#
# Copy this file to the project root as `.worktreeinclude` and edit the
# entries for the project's actual local files. Comments (lines starting
# with #) and blank lines are ignored.

.env
.env.local
